rows.en:
...Come to think of it, ever since I left the house, the doll hadn't left {f:my|my} side.
Maybe it was watching {f:me|me}; it felt like the gap between it and {f:me|me} was slowly closing.
Did that mean the end was {f:near|near}?{p}

{f:I|I} didn't have any time {f:left|left}.
There was no room to {f:hesitate|hesitate} here.
{f:I|I} turned the knob and opened the heavy wooden door.{p}

...No {f:good|good}.
It was locked.
It was sturdily made, and there was no way I could break it open.{p}

November 14.
The doll arrived, but it looks nothing like Shoji.
I have had it sent back to be made again.{p}

December 18.
I have asked doll maker after doll maker and had every kind of doll made, but none of them satisfies me.
What I want is a perfect doll.{p}

"...Welcome."
Standing beyond the door was the man from the portrait.
It was the {f:principal|principal}.{p}

He was gripping a golf club in his hand.
"...Principal."
{f:I|I} murmured it without thinking.{p}

There was definitely something in there.
{f:I|I} shoved my hand into my pocket.
The key that had been tucked inside that {f:diary.|diary...}
That {f:had to|had to} be the key to this wardrobe.{p}
